    "annotations": [
      {
        "id": "a1",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Open loop.** Each ball gets the trim current of its gap and starts dh0 = 10 nm below it, at rest. The deviation grows as dh0*cosh(s*t); Grow*/lambda = v/(h - p) tends to the unstable pole s = sqrt(2*g/p): 19.81, 11.44 and 8.86 1/s.",
        "x": 960,
        "y": -40,
        "w": 420,
        "h": 120,
        "color": "green"
      },
      {
        "id": "a2",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Small step (0.15 -> 0.155 m).** The same frozen PID (0.15 m gains) and trim feedforward around the nonlinear ball (BallS) and around its linearisation at 0.15 m (LinS: A = [0 1; 2g/p 0], B = [0; -2 sqrt(g alpha/m)/p], C = [1 0] at p = 0.15 m, taking the absolute current and returning the absolute gap). DiffS = BallS/h - LinS/h stays below 0.5 % of the step.",
        "x": 1380,
        "y": 600,
        "w": 420,
        "h": 150,
        "color": "blue"
      },
      {
        "id": "a3",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Large step (0.15 -> 0.21 m).** The controller now asks for a negative current; the real force alpha*i^2/h^2 still pulls (it does not care about the sign), the linear model pushes. The real ball can at best fall freely, so it lags the linear one: DiffL reaches 18 % of the step.",
        "x": 1380,
        "y": 1020,
        "w": 420,
        "h": 130,
        "color": "pink"
      }
    ]
  },
